## Supervisor Review Summary — Round 67

### Experiment Reviewed: exp052 (Global Statistics 12-dim)
- **Verdict**: ❌ FAILED — Global stats hurt performance
- **Baseline Amp Corr**: 0.746 (30 tracks) / 0.878 (9 common URMP tracks vs exp033's 0.890 = **-0.012**)
- **Root cause**: 5 constant-per-frame global features ignored by GRU, and 12-dim input degraded encoder learning of core 7-dim features
- **Stage 2 training unstable**: Best at epoch 11/300, then loss spiked to 3.8

### Critical Issues Found (3)
1. **[C1] encoder.py input_dim=12 must revert to 7** — breaks all exp033-based experiments
2. **[C2] dataset.py 12-dim features must revert to 7** — shape mismatch with exp033 checkpoints
3. **[C3] TCNAmpPredictor.forward() missing kwargs** — will TypeError when called from train.py/evaluate.py (needs `**kwargs`)

### Next Plan: exp053 — TCN-based AmpPredictor
- **Key insight**: `TCNAmpPredictor` (WaveNet-style dilated CNN) is **already fully implemented** in diffusion.py, train.py, and evaluate.py — but has **never been tested in any experiment**!
- **Architecture change**: GRU+Attention → Dilated Conv stack (8 layers, dilations 1→128)
- **Why this might work**: Multi-scale parallel temporal modeling vs sequential GRU; better for smooth amplitude envelopes
- **Cost**: Fix 3 bugs, create config, train ~30 min
- **Expected**: 0.78-0.82 Amp Corr

